Backtrace the window geometry trace, and retire a red herring it exposed.

CIDER_WINGEOM printed the rect a window was asked for but not WHO asked. Four windows arrive 1x1
with a style mask matching no constant in this tree and a class of plain NSWindow rather than any
toolkit subclass, and for several sessions task #227 was titled around them: "Qt renders nothing,
the window is created 1x1 and never mapped".

ONE FRAME LIST ENDED THAT:

    -[NSWindow initWithContentRect:styleMask:backing:defer:]
      -[NSCachedImageRep initWithSize:depth:separate:alpha:]
        -[NSImage drawInRect:fromRect:operation:fraction:]
          qt_mac_toQPixmap(NSImage const*, QSizeF const&)
            qt_mac_toQBrush(NSColor const*, QPalette::ColorGroup)
              QApplicationPrivate::basePalette()

THEY ARE NOT APPLICATION WINDOWS. They are NSCachedImageRep offscreen backing, one per palette
brush Qt rasterises, and in this port a cached image rep allocates a window. So the headline of
that task was about something that was never going to be on screen, and the real failure, an
application that completes QApplication init and exits without showing anything, was being read
through the wrong lens.

WHAT IS LEFT OF IT IS SMALLER AND REAL: the rasterisation is 1x1 because Qt asks a non pattern
colour for its patternImage and this port hands back nothing to size from. That makes a brush a
1x1 texture where a colour was meant, which is a rendering defect rather than a startup one.

FOUR THINGS ELIMINATED WHILE GETTING HERE, so they are not re-derived: none of the 9 colours Qt
asks for answers nil; colorUsingColorSpace: IS implemented and never returns nil, it falls back
to self; NSColor_catalog colorSpaceName answers NSNamedColorSpace rather than NSPatternColorSpace;
and the screen Qt sees is correct since ef39f657.

